有多少人参加过之前的创新讲座？

9
00:00:17,915 --> 00:00:19,110
So, quite a few of you.
所以，你们当中有不少人。

10
00:00:19,110 --> 00:00:20,820
It's great to see you back.
很高兴再次见到你。

11
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:29,670
For those of you that haven't come, this is a talk where I cover innovations across the spectrum of everything
对于还没到场的各位，这是一场我将全面介绍 Azure 基础设

12
00:00:29,670 --> 00:00:38,070
in the Azure infrastructure, from data centers all the way to cybersecurity and the cyber systems that we've got under development in Azure.
施各个层面创新的演讲，从数据中心一直延伸到我们正在开发的网络安全和网络系统。

13
00:00:38,070 --> 00:00:43,290
One of the notes that I make about this is that I'm showing you things, in some cases,
我在这里提到的一点是，我向你们展示的一些内容，

14
00:00:43,290 --> 00:00:47,640
that haven't shipped yet, some things that we're working on, some things that maybe have just shipped.
有些尚未发布，有些还在开发中，有些可能刚刚才发布。

15
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:55,150
For things that haven't shipped, they might not necessarily ever ship or ship in the same kind of view that you see me present them at.
对于那些尚未发布的产品，它们未必真的会发布，或者即使发布，也未必会以我展示给你的那种形态呈现。

16
00:00:55,175 --> 00:00:56,661
So that's just a caveat and takeaway.
所以，这只是个提醒和要点。

17
00:00:56,686 --> 00:01:04,410
But I thought it's fun to give you an under-the-hood look at what we're doing and what powers the infrastructure of Azure and Azure innovation.
但我认为，向大家展示我们正在做的事情，以及支撑 Azure 及其创新的基础设施背后的技术，挺有趣的。

18
00:01:04,410 --> 00:01:06,180
So let's start with infrastructure.
那我们先从基础设施开始。

19
00:01:06,180 --> 00:01:12,120
And you've seen these pictures of the Fairwater data centers.
你见过那些关于Fairwater数据中心的照片。

20
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:16,005
And this kind of sets a framework for a lot of the innovation that I'm going to be showing here,
这为我接下来展示的众多创新奠定了基础，这些创新聚焦于推

21
00:01:16,029 --> 00:01:25,410
which is innovation powering AI, specifically the co-design of AI data centers, the core infrastructure, and the software that runs on top of it.
动人工智能的发展，特别是人工智能数据中心、核心基础设施以及其上运行的软件的协同设计。

22
00:01:25,410 --> 00:01:28,260
I had a really awesome experience in November.
我十一月时经历了一次非常棒的体验。

23
00:01:28,260 --> 00:01:30,870
I got to go visit Fairwater in Atlanta.
我得去亚特兰大的费尔沃特看看。

24
00:01:30,870 --> 00:01:33,420
These are Fairwater in Wisconsin, Fairwater in Atlanta.
这是威斯康星州的费尔沃特，以及亚特兰大的费尔沃特。

25
00:01:33,420 --> 00:01:35,760
The Atlanta site is on the right.
亚特兰大站点在右侧。

26
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:43,486
And I got to go in to it, and I thought I'd show you a quick video tour of it, just a few seconds of me walking through it.
而且我有机会进去看看，我想给你们快速展示一下，就几秒钟我走一遍的视频。

27
00:01:43,511 --> 00:01:45,030
And I don't know why that didn't play.
我不知道为什么那段没放出来。

28
00:01:45,030 --> 00:01:50,790
Maybe I need to hit the play button up here.
也许我得点一下这里的播放按钮。

29
00:01:50,790 --> 00:01:53,340
So this is me looking like Builder Bob walking through.
这就是我像建造者鲍勃一样走着的样子。

30
00:01:53,340 --> 00:01:55,230
That's because it's under construction.
因为还在建设中。

31
00:01:55,230 --> 00:01:57,240
It's kind of continuously under construction.
它一直在持续建设中。

32
00:01:57,240 --> 00:02:04,980
This is the network cabling that connects the top floor servers and the bottom floor servers that goes up through trunks there, you can see.
这就是连接顶层服务器和底层服务器的网络布线，从那里穿过竖井向上延伸，你可以看到。

33
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:08,580
There's enough cabling to wrap the earth four times in one of these.
一个这样的机架里，电缆长度足以绕地球四圈。

34
00:02:08,580 --> 00:02:15,240
Those are liquid cooling cables being laid there initially so that servers can be dropped in.
那些是最初铺设的液冷电缆，以便后续直接放入服务器。

35
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:18,900
And you can see, we got to see one of these servers on the sled being racked.
你可以看到，我们看到其中一台服务器被安装到了导轨上。

36
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:22,590
These are the cables on the back, the InfiniBand and Ethernet cables.
这些是背面的线缆，包括 InfiniBand 和以太网线缆。

37
00:02:22,590 --> 00:02:25,200
And then you can see this is a brake fix that we got to watch.
然后你们可以看到，这是一个我们需要关注的刹车故障。

38
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:27,780
This is the liquid cooling into the back of the racks.
这是液体冷却系统进入机架背面。

39
00:02:27,780 --> 00:02:29,280
And then I saw this on the tour.
然后我在参观时看到了这个。

40
00:02:29,280 --> 00:02:31,440
The group had gone ahead of me.
那群人已经走在我前面了。

41
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:34,647
I saw a plug and I plugged it in.
我看到一个插头，就插上了。

42
00:02:36,277 --> 00:02:37,669
Because it's like, what's this?
这到底是什么？

43
00:02:37,694 --> 00:02:38,952
Shouldn't be hanging like that.
不该那样挂着。

44
00:02:38,977 --> 00:02:46,050
And Scott Guthrie got a text literally a few minutes later saying it looks like we've already powered on Power Cell 3.
几分钟后，斯科特·古休收到一条短信，说看起来我们已经成功启动了电源单元3。

45
00:02:46,050 --> 00:02:48,146
We didn't expect that.
我们没想到会这样。

46
00:02:48,171 --> 00:02:51,706
I wanted to take credit, but I thought maybe I best shouldn't for that.
我想把功劳揽过来，但转念一想，也许最好还是别这么干。

47
00:02:53,702 --> 00:02:56,994
But inside the data centers themselves, we've got the servers, of course.
但数据中心内部，我们当然有服务器。

48
00:02:57,019 --> 00:03:01,080
And one of the innovations that we've been developing in our servers is something called Azure Boost.
我们服务器中开发的一项创新技术叫做 Azure Boost。

49
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:12,360
Azure Boost is aimed at offloading a lot of the processing of the data paths for storage and networking off the main server CPUs.
Azure Boost 的目标是将存储和网络数据路径的大量处理任务从主服务器 CPU 上卸载出去。

50
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:14,790
And it does this with an offload card.
它通过一个卸载卡来实现这一点。

51
00:03:14,790 --> 00:03:18,450
We move the data planes off onto that offload card.
我们将数据平面转移到那个卸载卡上。

52
00:03:18,450 --> 00:03:20,550
We power them with DPUs.
我们通过数据处理单元为它们提供动力。

53
00:03:20,550 --> 00:03:24,180
We've got cores on there as well, where we put our agent tree.
我们也在上面放置了核心，用于部署我们的智能体树。

54
00:03:24,180 --> 00:03:32,850
So we get the agents off the server as well, and this lets the workload have most of the control over what's going on on the server.
因此，我们也将智能体从服务器上移开，这样工作负载就能对服务器上的大部分操作拥有主导权。

55
00:03:32,850 --> 00:03:34,500
This Azure Boost card looks like this.
这张 Azure Boost 卡看起来是这样的。

56
00:03:34,500 --> 00:03:38,440
This is the latest generation of Azure Boost card that we've started to deploy in our data centers.
这是我们已经开始在数据中心部署的最新一代 Azure Boost 卡。

57
00:03:38,465 --> 00:03:41,580
Here's an actual version of it right here.
这就是它的一个真实版本，就在这里。

58
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:46,380
And what you can see there, there's little black squares around the middle are D-RAM.
你可以看到，中间那些小黑方块是 D-RAM。

59
00:03:46,380 --> 00:03:48,420
And then the middle is where the SOC is.
中间部分就是系统级芯片（SOC）所在的位置。

60
00:03:48,420 --> 00:03:53,010
That's where the ARM cores and the DPU and FPGA are located.
这里就是 ARM 核心、数据处理单元和 FPGA 所在的位置。

61
00:03:53,010 --> 00:03:57,210
That's where the data plane gets processed and the agents run.
数据平面在这里进行处理，智能体也在此运行。

62
00:03:57,210 --> 00:04:00,510
Now some of the stats for Azure Boost are pretty staggering.
Azure Boost 的一些数据表现相当惊人。

63
00:04:00,510 --> 00:04:03,810
You can see here, just in last year,
你可以看到，仅在过去一年里，

64
00:04:03,810 --> 00:04:11,700
since the previous generation of Azure Boost that I showed at last Build, we've gone to 20 gigabytes per second of remote storage.
自去年 Build 大会上我展示上一代 Azure Boost 以来，远程存储速度已提升至每秒 20 吉字节。

65
00:04:11,700 --> 00:04:15,540
And that's an increase, you can see there, of 1.4.
可以看到，这增加了1.4。

66
00:04:15,540 --> 00:04:21,060
We've gone to 1 million IOPS for remote storage, and on local storage, 36 gigabytes per second,
我们已实现远程存储每秒100万次输入输出操作，本地存储则达到每秒36吉字节，这是针对本地NVMe的性能，

67
00:04:21,060 --> 00:04:29,224
this is to local NVMe, and 6.6 million IOPS through Azure Boost NVMe offload storage acceleration.
而通过Azure Boost NVMe卸载存储加速，可实现每秒660万次输入输出操作。

68
00:04:29,248 --> 00:04:33,260
And then for networking, we've gone to 400 gigabits from 200 gigabits.
而在网络方面，我们已从200吉比特升级到了400吉比特。

69
00:04:33,260 --> 00:04:41,910
So those were two network ports that you saw there on the card, 200 gigabits each, and 400k connections per second, it supports.
所以你看到的这张卡上有两个网络端口，每个端口速率为200吉比特，每秒支持40万次连接。

70
00:04:41,910 --> 00:04:50,370
Those two ports mean that they can go to two top-of-rack router switches, so that means that we can service top-of-rack routers, or if one fails,
这两个端口意味着它们可以连接到两台机架顶部的路由器交换机，因此我们可以为机架顶部的路由器提供服务，或者当其中一台出现故障时，

71
00:04:50,370 --> 00:04:52,375
we don't lose complete connectivity to the server.
也不会完全失去与服务器的连接。

72
00:04:52,400 --> 00:05:01,470
And it also means that sub-second servicing is possible now on those tours with sub-second impact to the workloads running on those servers.
这也意味着，现在可以在这些服务器上实现亚秒级的服务响应，对运行在这些服务器上的工作负载的影响也控制在亚秒级。

73
00:05:01,470 --> 00:05:07,260
We've been deploying this for several years now, and we're over 30% of the fleet is now Azure Boost enabled.
我们已经部署了这么多年，目前超过30%的车队已启用 Azure Boost。

74
00:05:07,260 --> 00:05:09,362
Every single server gets an Azure Boost in it.
每一台服务器都内置了 Azure 加速功能。

75
00:05:09,387 --> 00:05:16,020
And then one of the cool innovations that I'll show you in a little bit is that we support guest virtual machine RDMA.
接下来我要向大家展示的一个酷炫创新是，我们支持来宾虚拟机的RDMA。

76
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:25,616
So this is basically memory to memory transfers, bypassing the networking stacks, because Azure Boost is facilitating that transport.
所以这本质上是内存到内存的传输，跳过了网络栈，因为 Azure Boost 正在协助完成这一传输。

77
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:33,420
One of the things that I mentioned is we get the management services off the server, and we put them on the Azure Boost card.
我提到的一点是，我们将管理服务从服务器上移除，转而放到 Azure Boost 卡上。

78
00:05:33,420 --> 00:05:36,900
And that lets us have Bare Metal instances.
这使我们能够提供裸金属实例。

79
00:05:36,900 --> 00:05:46,110
We've introduced Bare Metal instances to unlimited access, specifically for OpenAI and OpenAI's use of that Fairwater data center.
我们已推出裸金属实例，为 OpenAI 及其使用 Fairwater 数据中心的场景提供无限访问权限。

80
00:05:46,110 --> 00:05:50,790
So the servers in the data center, the GPU servers, are Bare Metal instances.
因此，数据中心中的服务器，也就是GPU服务器，都是裸金属实例。

81
00:05:50,790 --> 00:05:58,710
And I thought I'd show you just a quick demo of Bare Metal instances, which are going to be coming as a general purpose offering sometime in the near future.
我想给大家快速演示一下裸金属实例，它们将在不久的将来作为通用型产品推出。

82
00:05:58,710 --> 00:06:04,440
But here, you can see we've got a metal instance, ND144 v6.
但在这里，你可以看到我们有一个金属实例，ND144 v6。

83
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:06,810
You can see here we're going to get the IP address,
可以看到，这里我们会获取IP地址，

84
00:06:06,810 --> 00:06:19,050
and then we're going to SSH into it and actually see that it is a Bare Metal server, because we're going to look to see if virtualization services are running, and they're not.
然后通过SSH连接进去，实际查看它是否为裸金属服务器，方法是检查虚拟化服务是否在运行，而实际上它们并未运行。

85
00:06:19,050 --> 00:06:23,670
And then we're going to look at the PCI bus using LSPCI.
然后我们将使用 LSPCI 查看 PCI 总线。

86
00:06:23,670 --> 00:06:26,081
And you can see we get lots of devices.
你可以看到，我们获得了大量设备。

87
00:06:26,106 --> 00:06:29,790
We're going to scroll to the top, and you can see there's a PCI bridge,
我们将滚动到顶部，可以看到一个 PCI 桥接器，

88
00:06:29,790 --> 00:06:39,150
and then you can see the eight Ethernet controllers that are connected to the Mellanox RDMA-capable network adapters
接着可以看到连接到 Mellanox RDMA 兼容网络适配器的八个以太网控制器，

89
00:06:39,150 --> 00:06:45,360
that are attached to that for the backend network that those GPUs talk through to each other.
这些适配器连接到后端网络，供 GPU 之间通信使用。

90
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:46,770
Now what do they talk?
他们到底在聊什么？

91
00:06:46,770 --> 00:06:48,300
What transport do they talk?
他们说的是什么交通工具？

92
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:53,280
We switched to Ethernet from InfiniBand, actually, in those Fairwater data centers.
实际上，我们在费尔沃特数据中心改用以太网替代了 InfiniBand。

93
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:58,170
And instead of using RoCE, which is RDMA over converged Ethernet,
我们没有采用 RoCE（融合以太网上的 RDMA），

94
00:06:58,170 --> 00:07:03,840
we've developed, with OpenAI and now a growing consortium of partners that are collaborating with us,
而是与 OpenAI 以及越来越多的合作伙伴共同开发了一种新的网络协议，名为多路径可靠连接（Multi

95
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:09,060
a new networking protocol called Multipath Reliable Connection, or MRC.
path Reliable Connection，简称 MRC）。

96
00:07:09,060 --> 00:07:16,290
And the reason that we developed MRC is that when you talk about connecting 100,000 GPUs together,
我们开发 MRC 的原因在于，当谈到将十万块 GPU 连接在一起时，

97
00:07:16,290 --> 00:07:23,220
that's an incredible amount of network fabric that those packets are going across from all of those GPUs.
这些 GPU 之间传输的数据包所经过的网络规模是极其庞大的。

98
00:07:23,220 --> 00:07:31,305
If you have any congestion or any failure on a synchronous training job of that size, you're going to lose a ton of work.
如果你在如此规模的同步训练任务中遇到任何拥塞或故障，你将损失大量工作。

99
00:07:31,330 --> 00:07:36,660
You're going to have to go back to a checkpoint, restart the training job from where it left off.
你得回到一个检查点，从上次中断的地方重新启动训练任务。

100
00:07:36,660 --> 00:07:47,700
So MRC is designed to be resilient in the face of these congestion issues or failures because it sprays the packets across independent network domains called planes.
因此，MRC 被设计为在面对这些拥塞问题或故障时具备韧性，因为它会将数据包分散到称为“平面”的独立网络域中。

101
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:56,186
And therefore, when a link gets dropped, the spraying just happens and rebalances to the planes that remain available.
因此，当某个连接断开时，流量会立即重新分布，并自动均衡到其他可用的平面。

102
00:07:56,211 --> 00:08:02,560
And I'll show you a quick demo of that in action by showing you here.
接下来我将通过一个快速演示向您展示其实际运行效果。

103
00:08:04,530 --> 00:08:11,940
What we're going to see is that I've got two servers talking to each other over four switches.
我们将会看到，我有两台服务器通过四台交换机相互通信。

104
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:17,130
They're sending 4 gigabyte payloads to each other.
他们正互相发送4吉字节的数据包。

105
00:08:17,130 --> 00:08:21,570
These 4 gigabytes are going to be packet sprayed across these.
这4吉字节的数据将被分包并分散传输到这些设备上。

106
00:08:21,570 --> 00:08:30,270
And you can see we're getting roughly 95 gigabytes per second, and that's because we're spraying these across eight planes with 12 gigabits.
你可以看到，我们的传输速率大约达到了每秒95吉字节，这是因为我们将数据分散到八个平面，每个平面的带宽为12吉比特。

107
00:08:30,270 --> 00:08:33,660
So that comes out to 12 gigabytes per plane.
每架飞机对应12吉字节。

108
00:08:33,660 --> 00:08:39,076
And this is the aggregate bandwidth that we're seeing, which is 95 gigabytes per second.
这就是我们看到的总带宽，达到每秒95吉字节。

109
00:08:39,101 --> 00:08:47,160
This is what we're going to watch, because we want to maintain 95 gigabits per second there, which is our goal.
这就是我们要观察的内容，因为我们希望在那里保持每秒95吉比特的速率，这是我们设定的目标。

110
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:48,510
We see four switches.
我们看到四个开关。

111
00:08:48,534 --> 00:08:52,391
You can see how much bandwidth is being spread across the switches.
你可以看到有多少带宽被分配到了各个交换机上。

112
00:08:52,416 --> 00:09:00,570
There's actually two switches at this bandwidth here that you don't see, so this is 12, two 24s, and one 36, adding up to 95.
实际上在这个带宽上还有两个你没看到的开关，分别是12、两个24和一个36，加起来总共是95。

113
00:09:00,570 --> 00:09:03,150
And now we're going to go kill one of those switches.
现在我们要去把其中一个开关给关掉。

114
00:09:03,150 --> 00:09:07,260
We're going to drop it off of the sending server.
我们将把它从发送服务器上卸下。

115
00:09:07,260 --> 00:09:13,290
So what it's going to do is now rebalance the spraying across the remaining three switches.
它现在会重新分配剩余三个开关之间的喷洒。

116
00:09:13,290 --> 00:09:16,530
And our goal is to not see any drop in network bandwidth.
我们的目标是确保网络带宽不会有任何下降。

117
00:09:16,530 --> 00:09:18,780
And, of course, that's exactly what we get.
当然，这正是我们所得到的。

118
00:09:18,780 --> 00:09:22,156
You can see 95-ish gigabits per second.
你可以看到大约每秒95吉比特。

119
00:09:22,180 --> 00:09:27,330
And if we go take a look at the traffic over the switches, you can see that one of them went to zero,
如果我们查看一下交换机上的流量，可以看到其中一个降到了零，

120
00:09:27,330 --> 00:09:31,890
and then the other one went up to 36 gigabits per second to compensate for that.
另一个则上升到每秒36吉比特，以弥补这一缺口。

121
00:09:31,890 --> 00:09:42,678
So MRC is what allows us to run these massive training jobs and has now become the industry standard for large network topologies.
因此，MRC 让我们能够运行这些大规模的训练任务，如今已成为大型网络拓扑的行业标准。

122
00:09:44,680 --> 00:09:48,540
Now I mentioned RDMA a few times.
刚才我提到了几次 RDMA。

123
00:09:48,540 --> 00:09:56,160
And what I was showing you was MRC, which is what Open AI uses for their training jobs.
我刚才向你们展示的是 MRC，这是 OpenAI 用于训练任务的系统。

124
00:09:56,160 --> 00:10:00,570
And they're doing RDMA, of course, between the servers in those training jobs.
当然，他们在这些训练任务的服务器之间进行 RDMA。

125
00:10:00,570 --> 00:10:06,950
But what we want to introduce is to more general-purpose workloads RDMA through virtual machines.
但我们想介绍的是，通过虚拟机实现更通用的工作负载RDMA。

126
00:10:06,950 --> 00:10:16,806
Now when you talk between one VM and another VM through Azure Boost, they could be on different servers, you're going through these networking stacks.
现在，当你通过 Azure Boost 在两个虚拟机之间通信时，它们可能位于不同的服务器上，你需要经过这些网络栈。

127
00:10:16,830 --> 00:10:23,460
The application talks to TCP/IP, which talks to our MANA driver, the Microsoft Accelerated Network Adapter driver,
应用程序通过 TCP/IP 与我们的 MANA 驱动程序通信，该驱动程序是微软加速网络适配器驱动程序，

128
00:10:23,460 --> 00:10:27,900
which is the Azure Boost network adapter driver, and then it goes back up.
也就是 Azure Boost 网络适配器驱动程序，然后数据再向上返回。

129
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:33,120
And there's a lot of memory copy operations and a lot of synchronization happening through that.
而且有大量的内存复制操作，以及大量的同步操作在其中进行。

130
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:35,690
With RDMA, you bypass all that.
通过 RDMA，你可以绕过所有这些。

131
00:10:35,690 --> 00:10:40,220
So the application maps memories basically in the remote system,
因此，应用程序基本上会将内存映射到远程系统，

132
00:10:40,220 --> 00:10:45,560
can drop data right into its own local presentation of that,
可以直接将数据放入其本地的对应表示中，

133
00:10:45,560 --> 00:10:50,460
and Azure Boost takes care of sending that and dropping it in the memory on the other side.
而 Azure Boost 会负责将数据发送并存入另一端的内存中。

134
00:10:50,460 --> 00:11:00,540
And this completely eliminates a lot of that synchronization as well as the memory copies and all that software path that you get through those networking stack.
这样一来，就完全消除了大量同步操作，以及通过网络栈带来的内存拷贝和所有软件路径。

135
00:11:00,540 --> 00:11:07,020
So I'm going to show you a demo of virtual machine to virtual machine RDMA over Azure Boost.
接下来我将演示一下在 Azure Boost 上，虚拟机到虚拟机的 RDMA。

136
00:11:07,020 --> 00:11:12,363
The scenario here is common in AI workloads, where you're doing inference.
这里的场景在 AI 工作负载中很常见，即进行推理。

137
00:11:12,388 --> 00:11:17,010
And inference, you can break up into two parts: prefill and decode.
推理可以分为两个部分：预填充和解码。

138
00:11:17,010 --> 00:11:25,230
Prefill is taking your prompt and then getting the tokens from that prompt and the KV cache populated from that prompt.
预填充阶段会获取您提示词中的词元，并用该提示词填充键值缓存。

139
00:11:25,230 --> 00:11:30,750
And then decode starts to generate new tokens based off of that system of that prompt.
然后解码开始根据该提示的系统生成新的词元。

140
00:11:30,750 --> 00:11:37,320
So it's efficient and now common to split those into different server pools, so one pool for prefill,
因此，现在高效的做法是将它们分开部署到不同的服务器池中，

141
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:43,980
one pool for decode, because they both have different constraints when it comes to memory and compute.
一个用于预填充，一个用于解码，因为两者在内存和计算方面有不同的需求。

142
00:11:43,980 --> 00:11:53,105
So here, we're going to start this demo of... RDMA.
那么，现在我们开始这个 RDMA 的演示。

143
00:11:53,130 --> 00:11:56,790
So first, we're going to look at the performance over the TCP/IP stack.
首先，我们将查看 TCP/IP 协议栈上的性能表现。

144
00:11:56,790 --> 00:12:01,050
So here's the pre-filler server using TCP/IP.
这是使用 TCP/IP 的预填充服务器。

145
00:12:01,050 --> 00:12:07,050
Here's the decoder server, also using TCP/IP, the way we're launching it.
这是解码服务器，同样使用 TCP/IP 协议，也是我们启动它的方法。

146
00:12:07,050 --> 00:12:15,910
And then we're going to go run this vLLM benchmark that does this prefill decode load between those two servers.
然后我们将运行这个 vLLM 基准测试，它会在两台服务器之间执行预填充和解码负载。

147
00:12:17,250 --> 00:12:20,952
And then we're going to go take a look at our RDMA stats, which is in the bottom right.
然后我们去看一下 RDMA 统计数据，位于右下角。

148
00:12:20,977 --> 00:12:25,440
And you're going to see that they don't change as this workload runs, there's 460 send requests.
你会看到，在这个工作负载运行过程中，它们不会发生变化，共有460个发送请求。

149
00:12:25,440 --> 00:12:27,900
Just keep your eye on that one.
注意盯着那个就行。

150
00:12:27,900 --> 00:12:34,770
But then if you take a look at the performance, the token throughput, which is what we really want, is about 3,400.
但如果你看一下性能，也就是我们真正关心的词元吞吐量，大约是3400。

151
00:12:34,770 --> 00:12:41,580
The median time to first token, which is another important stat for inference, is 123,000.
首词元时间的中位数为123,000，这也是推理过程中的一个重要指标。

152
00:12:41,580 --> 00:12:51,570
But when we switch over to RDMA and use the MANA link for that, you can see there's the F1 Verbs Device Name as MANA 0.
但当我们切换到 RDMA 并使用 MANA 链路时，可以看到 F1 Verbs 设备名称显示为 MANA 0。

153
00:12:51,570 --> 00:12:57,360
We do the same thing on the decode server, MANA 0.
解码服务器上我们也做同样的事情，MANA 0。

154
00:12:57,360 --> 00:13:04,260
And then let's go take a look at the stats, and you can see 460, but this is going to change now, because we're running the RDMA test.
然后我们去看看统计数据，你看到是460，但现在会变了，因为我们正在运行RDMA测试。

155
00:13:04,260 --> 00:13:08,670
And it changed to 506 because we've sent a whole lot of packets now over to RDMA.
而且变成了506，因为我们现在已经通过RDMA发送了大量的数据包。

156
00:13:08,670 --> 00:13:12,810
And then we've almost doubled the throughput to 7637.
然后我们的吞吐量几乎翻了一倍，达到7637。

157
00:13:12,810 --> 00:13:19,470
And then you can see our mean time to first token has dropped to just 47,000 milliseconds.
然后你可以看到，我们的首词元时间已降至仅 47,000 毫秒。

158
00:13:19,470 --> 00:13:29,700
So that's the performance benefit of RDMA that we're deploying and using in our inference clusters behind Foundry, powered by Azure Boost.
这就是我们通过 Azure Boost 驱动的 Foundry 后端推理集群所部署和使用的 RDMA 所带来的性能优势。

159
00:13:29,700 --> 00:13:32,130
Okay, so let's take a look at our core now.
好，我们来看一下我们的核心。

160
00:13:32,130 --> 00:13:36,600
So that's kind of Fairwater infrastructure and some of the networking behind it.
这就是法沃特的部分基础设施，以及其背后的一些网络架构。

161
00:13:36,600 --> 00:13:38,580
Let's go take a look at the core.
我们去看看核心部分。

